---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-pew-intentions/20261107-01/';
type Row = { source_group: string; intended_house_pct: Record<string, number> };
const analysis: { rows: Row[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}intentions.json`, 'utf8'));
---

<section id="participation-panel-intentions" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="panel-intentions-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Independent historical panel · Pre-election intentions only</p>
		<h2 id="panel-intentions-title">National panel: validated prior participation, intended House choice</h2>
		<p>Pew Research Center interviewed 3,917 registered voters on September 28–October 4, 2026.
			The prior groups have <strong>record-validated 2024 participation</strong> and surveyed
			post-election candidate choice. This is stronger historical evidence than a new 2026-only
			recall, but <strong>not completed November 2026 voting or turnout</strong>.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Pew national House intentions by validated prior participation">
		<table>
			<caption>Among each prior-choice group in the current registered-voter sample.
				House intentions include leaners; not percentages of the full original 2024 coalitions.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Source prior-vote group</th><th scope="col">Intended D</th>
				<th scope="col">Intended R</th><th scope="col">Another candidate</th>
				<th scope="col">Not sure</th><th scope="col">Item nonresponse</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{analysis.rows.map(row => <tr data-pew-prior={row.source_group}>
				<th scope="row">{row.source_group}</th>
				{['D', 'R', 'Other', 'Not sure'].map(party =>
					<td data-pew-choice={party}>{row.intended_house_pct[party]}%</td>)}
				<td data-pew-nonresponse>Not published</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>The workbook omits no-answer responses. A rounded sum of 100 does not establish zero refusals;
		we do not renormalize or treat unsure respondents as nonvoters. Validation concerns
		<strong>participation, not administratively observed candidate choice</strong>.</p>
	<p><strong>No population switching or drop-off counts.</strong> Current registered voters are
		not the eventual 2026 electorate or everyone who belonged to either 2024 coalition.
		These intentions are not multiplied by November ballot totals. Separate demographic
		preferences do not supply demographic-by-prior-vote joints; no state, county or precinct
		estimates or subgroup design confidence intervals are inferred.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Methods, historical timing and complete selected inputs</summary>
		<p>The <a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2026/10/08/with-americans-in-a-sour-mood-democratic-voters-are-more-engaged-in-midterms/">October 8 report</a>
			describes historical choice collection in the month after the 2024 election; its exported
			workbook says the week after. We preserve both descriptions rather than assert exact
			interview dates. The questions usually insert district candidates, with source-documented
			generic-party exceptions; this is not a single named statewide House race.</p>
		<p><a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2026/10/08/midterms-2026-methodology/">ATP weighting</a>
			addresses recruitment, selection, nonresponse and attrition, and includes validated 2024
			turnout and choice benchmarks. It does not establish 2026 electorate composition.
			SSRS fielded this separate Pew panel; a shared contractor does not make it the SSRS
			Voter Poll sample. We apply no new historical reweighting.</p>
		<p>Whole percentages are publisher-rounded descriptives, not exact population probabilities.
			Prior-group bases and joint design intervals are not supplied in these tables; the
			overall registered-voter margin of error is not reused for these conditionals.
			The complete archive contains both selected broad groups, all published response values,
			explicit unknown nonresponse, source URLs and hashes, methods and exact code/tests/results.
			Native HTML, PDFs, figures, the full workbook and respondent records are not redistributed.</p>
		<p>Source: Pew Research Center, American Trends Panel Wave 200.
			Copyright 2026 Pew Research Center. Limited factual excerpts; analysis is not endorsed
			by Pew Research Center. <a href="https://www.pewresearch.org/about/terms-and-conditions/">Source terms</a>.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete selected panel intentions + inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}intentions.json`} download>Panel intentions + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Panel archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-panel-intentions { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
